{"_src":{"As an English learner, the larger vocabulary you have, the more success you may achieve.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Emma, an actress, has become a superstar because of her hard work and talent.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","He had to make a choice between staying with his parents and going abroad.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","He was injured in a traffic accident.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","His selfless act of kindness touched everyone's heart.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","It takes about half an hour to ride from this park to Shanghai Museum.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Keep your head above the water.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Leave the reference books behind, or you won't be able to think by yourself.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Mr. Johnson is always kind to his students and he really cares about them.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","My brother is living abroad.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","My head aches after studying for a long time.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Nowadays too many boys want to become actors.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Our school club offers various activities, such as singing, gardening, and robotics.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","She could feel an ache in her back.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","She ran across the field to catch up with her friends.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Sue has the ability to succeed in business.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","The actor who acted in the TV series last night became famous in his thirties.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","The manager impressed on his office staff the importance of keeping accurate records.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","The river measures about 30 metres across.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","They accepted responsibility for the accident.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","They took an active part in the singing competition yesterday.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","Think well before you act.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","This job requires a bachelor's degree or above.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text","You'd better not ask too many personal questions about someone's age and salary.":"google:en-US-Neural2-F:text"},"a":{"As an English learner, the larger vocabulary you have, the more success you may achieve.":"","Emma, an actress, has become a superstar because of her hard work and talent.":"","He had to make a choice between staying with his parents and going abroad.":"","He was injured in a traffic accident.":"","His selfless act of kindness touched everyone's heart.":"","It takes about half an hour to ride from this park to Shanghai Museum.":"","Keep your head above the water.":"","Leave the reference books behind, or you won't be able to think by yourself.":"","Mr. Johnson is always kind to his students and he really cares about them.":"","My brother is living abroad.":"","My head aches after studying for a long time.":"","Nowadays too many boys want to become actors.":"","Our school club offers various activities, such as singing, gardening, and robotics.":"","She could feel an ache in her back.":"","She ran across the field to catch up with her friends.":"","Sue has the ability to succeed in business.":"","The actor who acted in the TV series last night became famous in his thirties.":"","The manager impressed on his office staff the importance of keeping accurate records.":"","The river measures about 30 metres across.":"","They accepted responsibility for the accident.":"","They took an active part in the singing competition yesterday.":"","Think well before you act.":"","This job requires a bachelor's degree or above.":"","You'd better not ask too many personal questions about someone's age and salary.":""}}
